# Kconfig  (drivers/npz2100)
# ---------------------------
# Configuration symbols for the nPZ2100 power-saving IC driver.
#
# Power architecture
# ------------------
# The nPZ2100 controls the nRF52833 host power switch (SW_HP).  When the
# nPZ2100 enters idle mode it cuts power to the nRF52833 completely — there
# is no always-on interrupt line.  Every nRF52833 boot is a fresh start
# caused by the nPZ2100 re-asserting SW_HP.
#
# On each boot the driver must:
#   1. Read STA1–STA3 immediately to learn the wake-up reason.
#   2. Read back all nPZ2100 registers to sync the shadow.
#   3. Diff the desired regmap against the shadow; write only what changed.
#   4. Re-enter idle when done — nPZ2100 cuts power again.

config NPZ2100
	bool "Nanopower Semiconductor nPZ2100 power-saving IC driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_NANOPOWER_NPZ2100_ENABLED
	depends on I2C
	help
	  Enable the nPZ2100 power-saving IC driver.

	  The nPZ2100 autonomously manages up to 6 sensors over I²C/SPI and
	  controls the nRF52833 host power switch.  When idle, the nPZ2100
	  cuts power to the nRF52833 entirely.  On each nRF52833 boot the
	  driver reads the wake-up reason from STA1–STA3, syncs its register
	  shadow from the device, applies any changed configuration, and
	  re-enters idle when the application is done.

if NPZ2100

config NPZ2100_INIT_PRIORITY
	int "nPZ2100 driver initialisation priority"
	default 80
	help
	  Zephyr device initialisation priority.  Must be higher (numerically)
	  than the I²C controller priority (typically 50–70) so the bus is
	  ready before the nPZ2100 driver runs.

module = NPZ2100
module-str = nPZ2100
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # NPZ2100
